==English==
[[File:Flickr - Official U.S. Navy Imagery - Recruits perform with a ceremonial honor guard..jpg|U.S Navy cadets performing  a ''shoulder arms (right)'' position.|thumb]]
[[File:Ernesto Antonio Dueñas Azucena inspects the Guard of Honour.jpg|New Zeland guards of honour in ''shoulder arms'' position.|thumb]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-shoulder arms.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|*}}

# {{lb|en|military}} a [[position]] or [[command]] in the [[manual]] of arms in which one places a [[rifle]] on the either [[left]] or [[right]] shoulder, with the [[forearm]] [[parallel]] to the ground and the [[hand]] holding the [[butt]].
#: {{cot|en|slope arms<qq:UK & Commonwealth>}}
# {{lb|en|Commonwealth|military}} a military command in which one places a rifle in the side of the flank and [[gripped]] by either left or right hand.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|military}} Of a soldier at drill, to place a [[rifle]] on the [[right]] shoulder, with the [[forearm]] [[parallel]] to the ground and the [[hand]] holding the [[butt]].
#: {{cot|en|slope arms<qq:UK & Commonwealth>}}
# {{lb|en|Commonwealth|intransitive|military}} Of a soldier at drill, to place a [[rifle]] in the side of the flank and [[gripped]] by either left or right hand.
# {{lb|en|intransitive|cricket}} To [[deliberately]] lift the [[bat]] out of the [[path]] of the [[ball]] when it is [[judged]] to be [[missing]] the [[wicket]].